   "text": "I read the molecule as an EZH2\u2011inhibitor warhead joined through a linker to a VHL ligand, and wrote the SMILES in those three parts.\n\n- **EZH2 end:** a 4,6\u2011dimethyl\u20112\u2011pyridone is attached through a CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O) amide to a toluamide ring. That ring carries an N\u2011ethyl\u2011N\u2011(tetrahydropyran\u20114\u2011yl)amino group and a para\u2011substituted phenyl group.\n- **Linker:** the phenyl group bears a CH2\u2013piperazine. The second piperazine nitrogen carries CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH, followed by five CH2 groups and a C(=O) that joins the VHL ligand. I counted the five CH2 groups from the zigzag spacing in the drawing.\n- **VHL end:** a tert\u2011leucine residue is acylated onto a 4\u2011hydroxyproline, whose carboxyl forms an amide with 4\u2011(4\u2011methylthiazol\u20115\u2011yl)benzylamine.\n\nThe drawing shows wedges and hashes at three stereocentres. I took these as the usual VHL\u2011ligand configuration, S for tert\u2011leucine and (2S,4R) for hydroxyproline. I then checked that the @/@@ marks in my SMILES give those same configurations.\n\nSMILES: CCN(C1CCOCC1)c1cc(-c2ccc(CN3CCN(CC(=O)NCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@H]4C(=O)NCc4ccc(-c5scnc5C)cc4)C(C)(C)C)CC3)cc2)cc(C(=O)NCc2c(C)cc(C)[nH]c2=O)c1C"
  }
